# Starting point only. Caddy starts with its own admin API on a unix socket and serves nothing; the
# admin pushes the real configuration (Network settings) through that socket when it starts, and
# `--resume` brings back the last one after a restart. A test keeps this file and the admin's copy
# (`bootstrap_caddyfile` in services/admin/src/caddy.rs) the same.
{
	admin unix//run/caddy/admin.sock|0660
}
